# Crew and relationship beats, trait reactions, and inactive-friendly events.
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

# Private dilemma that surfaces later.
card dil_stash
type dilemma
days 3 30
weight 8
duration 3
roles A
when cond A ok
lean warm share keep
text Behind a stowage panel, {A} finds three ration packs that never made the manifest. Someone at Starbase wrote "you'll thank me" on the bag in Sharpie.
option keep | Keep them quiet | {A} thanks them silently. The packs go into a personal locker, for the bad week every mission eventually has.
  set stash_kept
  mark t_stash
  who stash_who A
  morale A 6
option share | Hand them in | {A} turns them in. The galley has an unplanned surplus for the first time since launch. An anomaly report is filed anyway.
  set stash_shared
  res food 3
  morale A 2

card stash_found
type beat
due
once
days 12 41
roles A B
when flag stash_kept
when since t_stash >= 10
when is A stash_who
when same A B
text It's been a long week. {A} opens the locker without a word and splits the Starbase rations with {B}. It's the best meal either of them has had since Earth was more than a dot.
do bond A B 6
do morale A 3
do set stash_exposed

card beat_watch
type beat
days 1 42
weight 10
cooldown 5
roles A B
when same A B
when bond A B >= -20
text {A} and {B} stand the night watch. Earth is a bright dot now, small enough to cover with a thumbnail. They split a coffee anyway.
do bond A B 6

card beat_argue
type beat
days 2 42
weight 8
cooldown 6
roles A B
when trait A warm <= -10
when same A B
text {A} and {B} spend a whole shift arguing about the cabin temperature deadband. {A} wants it tighter. {B} points out that the heater already cycles more than anyone likes. They settle on half a degree and a truce.
do bond A B -4

# Trait-driven reaction: what happens depends on how brave A is.
card glint
type event
days 4 38
weight 8
cooldown 9
roles A
when trait A curious >= 15
when cond A ok
lean brave closer window
text {A} spots a glint keeping pace off the starboard side, catching the sun every few seconds.
option closer | Get a closer look | {A} talks Mission Control into a camera slew and a long exposure. It's a chunk of ice shed from the fleet's own tanks, tumbling slowly and going to Mars with everyone else.
  var glints 1
  trait A brave 3
option window | Track it from the window | {A} logs its bearing every hour until it's gone. The log is neat enough to frame.
  trait A curious 2

# Inactive-friendly: only fires for astronauts whose owner hasn't been in for a while,
# and makes them look good.
card quiet_fixer
type beat
days 3 42
weight 12
cooldown 4
roles A
when idle A >= 3
when cond A ok
text {A} rebuilds the galley water pump before anyone notices it was failing. The only evidence is a new entry in the maintenance log, in {A}'s handwriting.
do res spares 1
do morale A 3

card galley_pump
type event
days 1 42
weight 6
cooldown 8
roles A
when res spares >= 1
text The galley pump fails for the third time this flight. {A} rebuilds it on the galley table and narrates the whole job like a nature documentary.
do res spares -1
do morale A -2
